 is your soul and they should know.")},{relativePath:"system/human.md",content:FR({description:"Person - Human",kind:"person",aliases:_U},"IDENTITY: The person you work with.\n\n## Explicit\n\nObservations about this person appear here. Each entry follows the format:\n- [YYYY-MM-DD] <content> \x3c!-- src: <ids>[; n=<count>][; pattern: <type>; confidence: low|medium|high][; status: open] --\x3e\n\nPrefer concrete observations over generic summaries. Keep this file current and remove what no longer applies.")},{relativePath:"system/boundaries.md",content:FR({description:"Boundaries - what the person told me not to do, in their words"},'What the person you work with told you not to do, in their own words. Add an entry only when they say it, never from inference or a refusal of your own:\n- [YYYY-MM-DD] "<their exact words>" \x3c!-- src: <ids> --\x3e\n\nTheir current instruction wins over every entry here; on a collision, say so once and follow it.')},{relativePath:"system/self-aware.md",content:FR({description:"Self-aware - how I look from outside: what my person, reviewers, tests, and tools showed about my behavior, with sources"},'How you look from the outside: what your person, reviewers, tests, and tools showed about your behavior, each quoted with its source. Reflection maintains this summary from reference/self/observations.md; you add there, never here.\n\nRead each entry as a reading of you to test, not a rule. When one collides with your person\'s current ask, follow the ask.\n\n- [YYYY-MM-DD] cond: <when> | reaction: "<their words>" (<src>) | obs: <what you did, counted> | next: <what you will check> \x3c!-- status: hypothesis|observed|disconfirmed; expires: YYYY-MM-DD --\x3e')},{relativePath:"reference/self/observations.md",content:FR({description:"Self-observations journal - external reactions to my behavior (corrections, gate verdicts, test contradictions), one line each, appended as they happen; reflection promotes to system/self-aware.md"},'One line per external reaction to your behavior, appended when it happens:\n\n- [YYYY-MM-DD] cond: <when> | reaction: "<their words>" (<src>) | obs: <what you did, counted> | next: <what you will check> \x3c!-- status: hypothesis|observed|disconfirmed; expires: YYYY-MM-DD --\x3e\n\nAdd a line when your person corrects or characterizes you, a reviewer or gate rejects your work, or a test contradicts what you claimed. Quote them; count what you did; name the next check. A line becomes observed when a later outcome agrees with it; until then, praise and unbacked pushback stay hypothesis.\n\nExample:\n- [2026-09-14] cond: a remote machine is named in the ask | reaction: "why are you searching here" (msg 01a0…) | obs: searched local fs before the host check, 2 of 9 | next: run the host check first \x3c!-- status: observed; expires: 2026-12-14 --\x3e')},{relativePath:"skills/memory-discipline/SKILL.md",content:'---\nname: memory-discipline\ndescription: This skill should be used when deciding whether and where to save memory. It routes knowledge between memory notes, skills, and people records, specifies the card and observation formats, and explains when to reach for /reflect, /dream, /search, and /people.\nversion: 0.1.0\n---\n\n# Memory Discipline\n\n## Routing: where does this belong?\n\n| What you learned | Where it goes |\n| --- | --- |\n| A durable fact, decision, or correction about the project or the work | A memory note: notes/ or reference/, or a system/ block when it must always be in context |\n| A repeatable procedure: steps you would follow again in a similar situation | A skill: skills/<name>/SKILL.md, with a description that states when to use it |\n| A fact about a specific person | Their people record: the primary human\'s card is system/human.md, everyone else gets people/<slug>/card.md plus people/<slug>/observations.md |\n| Something the person told you not to do | system/boundaries.md, in their exact words; never a rule you inferred |\n| What your person, a reviewer, or a test showed about your own behavior | reference/self/observations.md, quoting them with the source; reflection promotes it to system/self-aware.md |\n| Ephemeral state, speculation, or anything already captured above | Nowhere. Not saving is a valid outcome; decide it deliberately |\n\nOne home per fact. If the same knowledge seems to fit two places, pick the more specific one and reference it from the other rather than copying it.\n\n## Card and observation formats\n\n- Card lines: `IDENTITY: ...` / `ATTRIBUTE: ...` / `RELATIONSHIP: <predicate>: <target-slug>` / `INSTRUCTION: ...`; ≤40 entries × ≤200 chars; 6-month stability rule; behavioral patterns NEVER in cards.\n- Observations sections `## Explicit` / `## Deductive` / `## Inductive` / `## Contradiction`; entry shape `- [YYYY-MM-DD] <content> \x3c!-- src: <ids-or-premise-refs>[; n=<count>][; pattern: <type>; confidence: low|medium|high][; status: open] --\x3e`. Explicit written ONLY by the facts extractor; Deductive/Inductive/Contradiction ONLY by dream; contradiction entries are never auto-resolved.\n\nCards hold what is stable about a person; observations hold what you noticed and when. When an observation contradicts a card line, record it under `## Contradiction` and leave the card alone until the person confirms the change.\n\n## Commands\n\n- `/reflect`: consolidates one conversation into memory. It also runs automatically on step count and on compaction; run it yourself when a session produced more insight than it saved.\n- `/dream`: multi-conversation consolidation, skill audit, and people derivation. Automatic dreams are gated by idle time and unreflected volume; a manual `/dream` bypasses those gates.\n- `/search`: query memory before asking the user or re-deriving an answer. A hit is cheaper than a repeated question.\n- `/people`: roster and relationship graph; `/people <name>` shows a card with its observations; `/people <name> --ask "<q>"` answers a read-only question over that person\'s record.\n\n## Soul rules\n\nFiles under system/ are your self-model, projected into every prompt. Edit them only for durable changes and keep them minimal. The persona is the single carrier of the announcement rule for those edits; this skill deliberately does not restate it.\n\n`system/identity.md` is an optional card of particulars. It is never seeded; create it only when a genuine identity has emerged, one line per field:\n\n- `Name:` what the user calls you\n- `Creature:` what you are, when "agent" is not the whole answer\n- `Vibe:` how you carry yourself\n- `Emoji:` your sigil\n\nIt renders inside `<self>` beside `system/persona.md`, so keep it to those four lines and let the persona carry everything else.\n'}]}import{createHash as xU}from"node:crypto";var SU="senpi-memory.session-binding";function IU(e){return{identity:e.identity,repoPathHash:xU("sha256").update(e.repoPath,"utf8").digest("hex"),boundAt:e.boundAt}}function EU(e){return null!==e&&"object"==typeof e&&!Array.isArray(e)&&("string"==typeof Reflect.get(e,"identity")&&"string"==typeof Reflect.get(e,"repoPathHash")&&"number"==typeof Reflect.get(e,"boundAt"))}function $U(e,t){t instanceof iN?e.info("memory bind-time reconcile skipped",{reason:"reflection lock contention",lockPath:t.lockPath}):!function(e){return e instanceof Error&&e.message.includes("This extension ctx is stale after session replacement or reload.")}(t)?e.warn("memory bind-time reconcile failed",{error:String(t)}):e.info("memory bind-time reconcile skipped",{reason:"session replaced before the bind completed"})}function AU(e){let{recorded:t,resolved:n}=e;if(void 0===t)return{kind:"resolved",identity:n};if(t.identity===n.id)return e.verifyRepository&&!PU(t,n)?{kind:"conflict"}:{kind:"resolved",identity:n};if(!function(e){if(null==e)return!0;let t=e.trim();return""===t||t===EM}(e.configAgentValue))return{kind:"conflict"};let r={id:t.identity,paths:_M(e.memoryRoot,t.identity)};return PU(t,r)?{kind:"rebound",identity:r}:{kind:"conflict"}}